ould cause you illnesses or other  problems and the only way to get rid of  those problems was to call a ritual  specialist an ashipu or Exorcist that  could use his specialized knowledge and  the tools that he had at his disposal to  get rid of the issue some of this we  recognize very clearly from our modern  conception of these things from how  ghosts work to demons and exorcisms but  we should also be careful not to project  are modern ideas onto a context in  ancient times that was very different a  lot of these Concepts and ideas have a  different meaning to the ancient  Mesopotamians than they perhaps do to us  today but at the very least it remains a  fascinating tradition of occult practice  a fascinating tradition of ancient  religion that not only can tell us a lot  about the development of these kinds of  ideas all the way to modern times but  also of course fits perfectly into this  wonderful yearly tradition of shocktober  here on let's talk religion as I said in  the beginning this is a collaboration  with three other creators again Dr  Justin Sledge from esoterica who will be  making a video about the dibik the very  famous kind of possessing uh spirit of  Judaism and especially or particularly  he will be talking about the first case  of dybic exorcism in the I believe the  16th century and that's incredibly  fascinating and of course connected to  what we talk about here so I'll have  talked just now about ancient exorcism  the earliest examples of exorcistic  rituals in ancient Mesopotamia and  Justin will be talking about how that  tradition is also present to some degree  in Judaism with the case of the dybic so  check out that video Dr Angela puka from  Angela Symposium will be making a video  about ancestor worship again very  strongly connected to a lot of what  we've been talking about here today uh  incredibly interesting stuff so check  out that video and then a trail aka the  modern hermeticist will basically be  putting out a full audiob